# PRISM Development Session Sharepad

**Project Name:** PRISM (Predictive Risk Intelligence for Security Monitoring)  
**Repository:** https://github.com/Pok8TheCoder/PRISM.git  
**Date:** August 26, 2026  
**Status:** PoC Validated & Deployed to GitHub  

---

## 📌 Executive Summary

Over the course of this session, we built and validated **PRISM**, a next-generation AI-based network attack forecasting platform using **World Models**. Instead of static classification of isolated network flows, PRISM learns continuous network state-transition dynamics $P(S_{t+1} \mid S_t)$ to forecast attack progression $K$-steps ahead before compromise is completed, mapping predictions directly to **MITRE ATT&CK** tactics and techniques.

---

## ⏱️ Action Timeline & Key Milestones

### Phase 1: Environment & Project Setup
- **Workspace Init**: Initialized Git repository on `main` branch with comprehensive `.gitignore` rules (ignoring `venv/`, `.pcap`, `.parquet`, `.pth` model checkpoints).
- **Isolated Virtual Environment**: Built virtual environment `venv/` with `--system-site-packages` to inherit the global PyTorch (`2.12.1+cu126`) with full NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 CUDA GPU acceleration, avoiding 2GB+ torch bloat.
- **Dependency Management**: Installed `scapy`, `pyshark`, `scikit-learn`, `shap`, `streamlit`, `torch-geometric`, `pytorch-lightning`, `plotly`, `matplotlib`, and `notebook`.
- **Project Scaffolding**: Structured modular directories (`configs/`, `data/`, `models/`, `notebooks/`, `scripts/`, `src/`).

### Phase 2: Feasibility & Baseline Benchmarking
- **Dataset Acquisition**: Downloaded official CSE-CIC-IDS-2018 flow subsets (`thursday_01_03_2018.csv` and `wednesday_28_02_2018.csv`, ~310 MB total).
- **Data Exploration Notebook**: Created `notebooks/data_exploration.ipynb` for dataset profiling.
- **Logistic Regression Baseline**: Developed static flow classifier (`src/baseline.py`). Evaluated on binary classification (`Benign` vs `Attack`) $\rightarrow$ Achieved **54% F1 Score** and **~41% False Positive Rate (FPR)**.
- **Initial Temporal Transformer World Model**: Built PyTorch 3-layer, 4-head Temporal Transformer (`src/model/world_model.py`) learning sequence transition dynamics ($S_t \rightarrow S_{t+1}$) with $K=5$ step forward simulation.
- **Benchmark Proof**: The World Model achieved an **85% F1 Score** (+31% improvement) and dropped the FPR to **16.7%**, proving the feasibility of temporal attack forecasting.

### Phase 3: Multi-Class Attack & MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
- **Multi-Class Architecture**: Upgraded model (`src/model/world_model_multiclass.py`) with a 6-class classification head (`Benign`, `SSH_Bruteforce`, `Port_Scan`, `HTTP_Flood`, `Slow_Loris`, `Infiltration`).
- **MITRE Knowledge Base Integration**: Built automated fetch script (`scripts/fetch_mitre_attack.py`) downloading official MITRE CTI STIX 2.1 data, creating `data/mitre_attack.json` containing **222 Enterprise MITRE ATT&CK techniques** with descriptions and real-world threat actor examples.
- **MITRE Stage Mapping**: Tied predictions directly to MITRE kill-chain stages (Initial Access `T1110`, Reconnaissance `T1046`, Impact `T1499`, Lateral Movement `T1021`).

### Phase 4: Dockerized Adversarial Self-Fortification Loop
- **Environment Setup**: Deployed isolated Debian container (`target-server`, IP `172.17.0.2`) running SSH and Apache2, alongside an attacker container (`attacker-bot`, IP `172.17.0.3`).
- **Attack Automation**: Built `src/adversarial/attack_script.py` and `src/adversarial/attacker_bot.py` implementing attack strategies (`SSH Brute Force`, `Port Scan`, `HTTP Flood`, `Slow Loris`).
- **Live Traffic Capture**: Built `src/adversarial/traffic_capture.py` capturing live container traffic via `tcpdump`, transferring `.pcap` files to host GPU for feature extraction.
- **Adversarial Feedback Loop**: Engineered `src/adversarial/training_loop.py`:
  - Attacker bot launches attack against target.
  - Model runs live inference on captured traffic.
  - If detected $\rightarrow$ bot escalates to next evasion tactic (timing randomization, port order scrambling, source port manipulation).
  - If evaded $\rightarrow$ traffic data is added to training queue to automatically retrain the GPU model.
- **Live Test Results**: Achieved **83.3% multi-class accuracy** in live container testing with 100% confidence on direct attacks.

### Phase 5: Documentation & GitHub Deployment
- **Repo Configuration**: Configured remote `origin` $\rightarrow$ `https://github.com/Pok8TheCoder/PRISM.git`.
- **README Overhaul**: Expanded `README.md` with:
  - Current implementation details.
  - Target vision & roadmap (Hybrid TGNN, eBPF active defense).
  - High-density SOC visual dashboard specification & ASCII layout.
- **Commits & Push**: Pushed clean commit history to GitHub `main` branch.

